        "ae1d09e9fa9752552300552c0a3e284094d627bd"
      ],
      "title": "Clear queued rescans when opening a file",
      "message": "Clear queued rescans when opening a file\n\nredissection_queued shouldn't be set when opening a file, but\nmake sure it's cleared. Otherwise things can enter a state where\nthe filter can't be changed or a redissection performed. cf_close\nalready checks the read lock and aborts if it's set, but it doesn't\nhurt to clear it for a newly opened file.\n\nWhen doing a cf_read, if there's a queued redissection at the\nstart of cf_read (which also shouldn't happen for similar reasons),\nclear it for the same reason as clearing it at the start of\nrescan_packets. The dissection in cf_read will satisfy any\npending request (and use the new filter.)\n\nThere's currently an issue with requesting a rescan (filtering,\nredissection) when in the middle of retapping or other functions\nthat hold the read lock.\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2024-04-09T08:45:05.000-04:00",
      "committer_name": "AndersBroman",
      "committer_email": "a.broman58@gmail.com",
